"""Q22: add Q22 entries to /output/report.json (idempotent). Numbers from out/q22/*.json. Usage: python3 -I s136_update_report_q22.py"""
import json
p='/output/report.json'; d=json.load(open(p)); R=d['results']
R[:]=[x for x in R if not x['quantity'].startswith('Q22:')]
d['recipe']=[x for x in d['recipe'] if not x['description'].startswith('Q22:')]
d['caveats']=[x for x in d['caveats'] if not x.startswith('Q22:')]
A=lambda n,v:{'name':n,'value':v}
T=json.load(open('/workspace/out/q22/s135.json'))
tb=lambda r:f"{T[r]['I_adopted']:.2f}+-{T[r]['stat']:.2f}(stat)+-{T[r]['sys_half_range']:.2f}(sys, range {T[r]['range'][0]:.2f}-{T[r]['range'][1]:.2f})"
v1=("The negative ramp at the low-frequency edge of Xb55 spw22 (163.244 GHz; first ~100 channels of 1.953 MHz, ~200 MHz, -3.5 to -5 mJy/beam in the first 10 channels at N, S, Bridge, relaxing roughly linearly to ~0 at channel ~140-170, where the CH3OH blend starts at ch~120) is a CONTINUUM-PROPORTIONAL, EDGE-LOCALISED residual of the pipeline continuum subtraction, not emission and not a property of the sky. "
 "Evidence (Xb55 pbcor peak-pixel spectra, noise 2.1 mJy/beam per channel, x1.3 for channel correlation): (a) amplitude over ch 0-30 vs continuum (line-free cont image, 14.3/12.7/14.9/6.9/4.4/-0.4/-0.5 mJy/beam at N/S/Bridge/E1/W/E2/Sblue) fits -0.21+-0.02 x continuum (through origin; chi2 23/6 with E1 an outlier, ~0 at E1); over ch 0-100 -0.157+-0.011 x continuum (chi2 16/6); zero at the continuum-free E2 and Sblue. (b) it exists only at the low-frequency edge: the high-frequency edge of spw22 is 0.0+-0.03 x continuum in the same pixels, and spw16 and spw20 (both edges) are 0+-0.04 x continuum in the same pixels, with the same continuum. (c) Same sign and size at the low edge of spw18 (-0.10 to -0.15 x continuum over the first ~80 channels, stacked N/S/Bridge), so it is spw-specific, not position-specific. (d) The sky-frequency overlap of spw20 (low edge) and spw22 (high edge), 164.54-165.11 GHz, agrees (spw22-spw20 = +0.14+-0.44, +0.13+-0.40, +0.11+-0.51 mJy at N/S/Bridge), so the baseline is not a sky feature; the ramp is not covered by any other spw. "
 "Interpretation: an amplitude roll-off of the continuum at the spw edge (bandpass/edge response) that the low-order continuum model of the delivered products does not follow leaves -(15-25)% of the continuum as a negative residual; since it scales with the continuum and is absent at other edges it is a continuum-subtraction residual caused by the edge response, and its amplitude at the CH3OH blend depends on how it is extrapolated across the line (ch 120-190). It is not a CH3OH red wing (negative, and it scales with continuum).")
R.append({'quantity':'Q22: origin of the negative ramp at the Xb55 spw22 low-frequency edge that sets the CH3OH blend baseline','target':'Xb55 spw22 (and spw16/18/20 as controls), N, S, Bridge, E1, W, E2, Sblue peak pixels','value':v1,
 'uncertainty':'ramp/continuum -0.21+-0.02 (ch 0-30), -0.157+-0.011 (ch 0-100); stat per channel 2.1 mJy/beam','unit':'fraction of continuum; mJy/beam',
 'assumptions':[A('continuum','line-free spw16_18_20_22 cont image pbcor at each region pixel; flat over the 1.9 GHz spw (alpha~1.5 changes it by <1%)'),A('noise','2.1 mJy/beam per 1.953 MHz channel x1.3 correlation inflation (s18)'),A('ramp zero level','reference taken as spectrum zero; ch 60-120 median also compared (s131); HCO+ 2-1 wings contaminate the spw18 profile at ch>150, spw16 at ch>~100 near HCN'),A('not tested','whether the raw uv data have the edge roll-off (only image cubes available)')],
 'confidence':'medium','evidence':'scripts/s130_q22_edge_ramp.py, s131_q22_edges_allous.py, s132_q22_ramp_fit.py, s133_q22_template.py -> out/q22/s130-s133.*'})
v2=("Blend integral with the edge ramp modelled and removed (beam-aperture spectra, window +-200 km/s about the region centre, Jy/beam km/s; mean of three empirical baselines: R ramp linear fit ch0-100 extrapolated to its zero crossing + constant from the blue side, L straight line through ch 55-100 and 230-420 (J=4,5 masked), Q quadratic through ch 0-100 + 230-420; sys = half range over methods and windows +-150 to +-300 km/s): "
 f"N {tb('N')}; S {tb('S')}; Bridge {tb('Bridge')}; W {tb('W')}. Zero-baseline lower bound (data taken at face value): N 0.77, S 1.15, Bridge 1.19, W 0.43. "
 f"The baseline range shrinks from a factor 2.0-3.5 (the 5 baselines of s120b at +-400 km/s, which include the ramp in the integration window) to a factor {T['N']['new_range_ratio']:.2f}/{T['S']['new_range_ratio']:.2f}/{T['Bridge']['new_range_ratio']:.2f}/{T['W']['new_range_ratio']:.2f} (N/S/Bridge/W), i.e. half-range/adopted = +-{T['N']['sys_half_range']/T['N']['I_adopted']*100:.0f}% (N), +-{T['S']['sys_half_range']/T['S']['I_adopted']*100:.0f}% (S), +-{T['Bridge']['sys_half_range']/T['Bridge']['I_adopted']*100:.0f}% (Bridge), +-{T['W']['sys_half_range']/T['W']['I_adopted']*100:.0f}% (W). The adopted values are within {abs(1-T['N']['scale_vs_old_median'])*100:.0f}/{abs(1-T['S']['scale_vs_old_median'])*100:.0f}/{abs(1-T['Bridge']['scale_vs_old_median'])*100:.0f}/{abs(1-T['W']['scale_vs_old_median'])*100:.0f}% (N/S/Bridge/W) of the earlier s120b medians. "
 f"Consequences for Q9: R_K(254/blend) S {T['S']['R_K']:.2f} ({T['S']['R_K_16_84'][0]:.2f}-{T['S']['R_K_16_84'][1]:.2f}) -> Trot {T['S']['Trot_16_50_84'][1]:.0f} K (16-84% {T['S']['Trot_16_50_84'][0]:.0f}-{T['S']['Trot_16_50_84'][2]:.0f}); Bridge R_K {T['Bridge']['R_K']:.2f} ({T['Bridge']['R_K_16_84'][0]:.2f}-{T['Bridge']['R_K_16_84'][1]:.2f}) -> Trot {T['Bridge']['Trot_16_50_84'][1]:.0f} K (16th percentile {T['Bridge']['Trot_16_50_84'][0]:.0f} K, upper end unbounded); N: 254 line 1 sigma, Trot unconstrained. Thin LTE, 254 line smoothed to the Xb55 beam, no beam-filling correction. "
 f"This tightens (but does not replace) Q9: S Trot ~{T['S']['Trot_16_50_84'][1]:.0f} ({T['S']['Trot_16_50_84'][0]:.0f}-{T['S']['Trot_16_50_84'][2]:.0f}) K versus 10 (+7/-5) K with the factor 2-4 baseline range; blend/HCO+ 2-1 ratios scale with the blend (S x1.08, Bridge x1.01, W x0.98, N x0.95), still equal within the +-40-80% errors. The remaining systematic is the extrapolation of the ramp across the line, and the CH3OH blend lies only ~120-190 channels from the spw edge, so the ramp cannot be separated from the line wing there.")
R.append({'quantity':'Q22: CH3OH J=1-3 blend integral and Trot at Xb55 with an empirical edge-ramp baseline (updates Q9 baseline systematic)','target':'N, S, Bridge, W (Xb55 beam aperture); Trot at S, Bridge','value':v2,
 'uncertainty':'blend systematic +-35% (N), +-24% (S), +-20% (Bridge), +-14% (W); stat +-0.07; Trot S 13 (10-20) K, Bridge median 30 K (>~17 K at 16%)','unit':'Jy/beam km/s; K',
 'assumptions':[A('baselines','R/L/Q as described; ramp assumed to be removed by the same continuum-scaled form under the line (linear extrapolation); zero baseline gives lower bound'),A('lines masked','J=4 (165.190, ch~219) and J=5 (165.369, ch~309) masked +-130 km/s in the baseline anchors; J=4 wing lies inside the +-250/300 km/s integration windows (non-detected, <~0.2 Jy/beam km/s)'),A('LTE inputs','same as s120c: 254.015 GHz Eu 20.1 K log A -4.72; blend 165.050/165.061/165.099 GHz')],
 'confidence':'medium','evidence':'scripts/s134_q22_blend_empirical.py, s135_q22_adopted_trot.py -> out/q22/s134.json, s135.json'})
d['recipe'].append({'description':'Q22: edge-ramp diagnosis in Xb55 spw16/18/20/22 (s130-s133), empirical baseline blend integral (s134), Trot propagation (s135), report (s136)','scripts':[f'/workspace/scripts/s13{k}.py' for k in ('0_q22_edge_ramp','1_q22_edges_allous','2_q22_ramp_fit','3_q22_template','4_q22_blend_empirical','5_q22_adopted_trot','6_update_report_q22')],'order':max(x['order'] for x in d['recipe'])+1,'stage':d['recipe'][-1]['stage']})
d['caveats'].append("Q22: the Xb55 spw22 low-edge negative ramp (-0.16 to -0.21 x continuum) is a continuum-proportional edge residual; with it modelled the CH3OH blend baseline systematic is +-14-35% (range factor 1.3-2.2, not 2-4) and Trot at S ~13 (10-20) K; the Q9 factor 2-4 statement applies to naive constant/linear baselines in +-400 km/s windows. Not verifiable without the uv data.")
